Task: Implementar el valor de la regla (Fase 2, pattern-copy_20260910)

Green phase. `PatternChord` takes `pressing(_:)`, `releasing(_:)` and
`cancelling(_:)` and answers `.none`, `.select(Int)` or `.copy(from:to:)`. It
keeps the fingers that are down in press order — the first is the copy origin —
plus one `spent` flag covering both ways a gesture can run out: it copied, or it
was cancelled. Neither selects on the way up.

The machine resets whenever the last finger lifts, whatever spent it. That is
the one thing the first attempt got wrong: it only reset on a selecting release,
so after a chord the flag survived into the next gesture and the following lone
tap selected nothing. `testTheNextGestureStartsFresh` caught it.

No `UIKit`, no `SwiftUI`, no stdlib-external import — `DependencyBoundaryTests`
still passes. It validates no indices either: the slot range belongs to `Bank`.

